    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>USER STORY:</b></p>

<blockquote><p>As a user, I want to return a product from a completed purchase invoice. After successfully returning the product, the returned quantity should be deducted from inventory, and all related purchase, reports, stock valuation, transactions, and profit calculations should be updated correctly.</p></blockquote>

<h3><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a><b>Acceptance Criteria</b></h3>

<h4><a name="1.FullProductReturn"></a><b>1. Full Product Return</b></h4>

<ul>
	<li><b>Given</b> a purchase invoice contains a purchased product,</li>
	<li><b>When</b> the user returns the entire purchased quantity,</li>
	<li><b>Then</b> the complete returned quantity should be deducted from stock.</li>
</ul>


<h4><a name="2.PartialProductReturnAfterPurchaseInvoice"></a><b>2. Partial Product Return After Purchase Invoice</b></h4>

<ul>
	<li><b>Given</b> a completed purchase invoice contains multiple products,</li>
	<li><b>When</b> the user returns only a portion of the purchased quantity,</li>
	<li><b>Then</b> only the returned quantity should be deducted from the stock.</li>
</ul>


<h4><a name="3.StockUpdate"></a><b>3. Stock Update</b></h4>

<ul>
	<li><b>Given</b> a product has been purchased and added to inventory,</li>
	<li><b>When</b> the user returns a portion of the purchased quantity,</li>
	<li><b>Then</b> the returned quantity should be deducted from the available stock.</li>
</ul>


<h4><a name="4.ReturnQuantityValidation"></a><b>4. Return Quantity Validation</b></h4>

<ul>
	<li><b>Given</b> a user has a completed purchase invoice,</li>
	<li><b>When</b> the user enters a return quantity greater than the available returnable quantity,</li>
	<li><b>Then</b> the system should reject the return and display an appropriate validation message.</li>
</ul>


<h4><a name="5.StockValuationUpdate"></a><b>5. Stock Valuation Update</b></h4>

<ul>
	<li><b>Given</b> the user has a completed purchase invoice,</li>
	<li><b>When</b> the user returns a product,</li>
	<li><b>Then</b> the system should update the stock valuation correctly based on the returned quantity.</li>
</ul>


<h4><a name="6.PurchaseAmountUpdate"></a><b>6. Purchase Amount Update</b></h4>

<ul>
	<li><b>Given</b> the user has purchased a product,</li>
	<li><b>When</b> the product is returned,</li>
	<li><b>Then</b> the purchase amount should be reduced correctly based on the returned quantity.</li>
</ul>


<h4><a name="7.ProfitUpdate"></a><b>7. Profit Update</b></h4>

<ul>
	<li><b>Given</b> a purchase invoice has affected the product's cost and profit calculation,</li>
	<li><b>When</b> a product is returned,</li>
	<li><b>Then</b> the system should recalculate the profit correctly based on the returned quantity and updated purchase cost.</li>
</ul>


<h4><a name="8.ReportsUpdate"></a><b>8. Reports Update</b></h4>

<ul>
	<li><b>Given</b> a purchase return has been completed,</li>
	<li><b>When</b> the user views inventory, purchase, stock valuation, or profit reports,</li>
	<li><b>Then</b> the reports should reflect the returned product and updated values correctly.</li>
</ul>

